      "math_academy_id": "e-9481",
      "problem": "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$",
      "worked_solution": "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
